1
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:25,780
YAMU!

2
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,477
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,880
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,460
Y 'all move!

5
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,180
Your turn, Yu-Gi-Boy.

6
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,257
But what's a poor Jueless to do?

7
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,557
If you throw your monsters in
defense mode, I'll fossilize them.

8
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,640
And if you throw them in
attack, I'll destroy them.

9
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,380
He's right. I'm trapped.

10
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,400
Unless maybe this combo works.

11
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,980
I'll play the Dark
Magician in attack mode.

12
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:23,900
Ooh, the Dark Magician.

13
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:29,180
And I also protect him
with the magical hats.

14
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,530
Brilliant!

15
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:39,057
Even Pegasus can't tell which hat
Yugi's hidden his Dark Magician in.

16
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:42,728
Now the Magician is safe from
Pegasus's toon monster attacks.

17
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,480
Ah, I see. See what?

18
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,857
With your feeble attempt
to hide your Dark Magician,

19
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:52,597
you're hoping to stall until you can
find a way to overcome my toon world.

20
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,500
But it won't work. Hmm?

21
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:56,540
Don't get it?

22
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:59,557
You're not capable of
concealing your secrets from

23
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:02,581
me and those silly magic
hats won't help you hide.

24
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:07,368
All I need to do is probe your feeble
mind to learn which hat hides your mage.

25
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:11,560
Or have you forgotten the
power of my millennium eye?

26
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,097
You might as well surrender now and save

27
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,004
yourself the embarrassment
of a crushing defeat.

28
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,477
Prepare yourself, Yugi boy.

29
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,120
Here I come.

30
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:28,420
What can I do if Pegasus reads my mind?

31
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,517
If he learns where the magician is?

32
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,430
I'm finished.

33
00:02:31,513 --> 00:02:33,437
There has to be some way I can stop him.

34
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,461
There has to be.

35
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,840
Yugi, come on, stay with it, man.

36
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:40,657
I know Pegasus has magic, but so do you.

37
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:43,740
The magic of your Millennium
Puzzle. That's it.

38
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:46,180
I do have my own kind of magic.

39
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:50,362
The magic that merges me with the
spirit of the Millennium Puzzle.

40
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,480
Spirit, listen to me. Quickly!

41
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:54,870
Yugi!

42
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,717
I can feel Pegasus trying to claw
his way into our minds again.

43
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,200
I can't keep him out!

44
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,160
I know, but I have an idea.

45
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,437
My grandpa told me that if
I wanted to defeat Pegasus,

46
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,057
I'd have to harness the power
of my Millennium Puzzle.

47
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:10,777
I thought that he meant I should
merge with you as we usually do,

48
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,137
and that together we would be triumphant.

49
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,900
But now I think I was wrong.

50
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:17,757
Grandpa said to trust in the
power of my Millennium Puzzle,

51
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,016
but he never said anything about you.

52
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,649
What are you saying, Yugi?

53
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:23,610
Spirit,

54
00:03:23,693 --> 00:03:25,797
if I'm to have any chance
of beating Pegasus,

55
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,527
I'm afraid I have to banish you
from the corridors of my mind.

56
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:40,380
Yugi, if we don't work together,
we won't stand a chance. Maybe not.

57
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:43,277
But if we keep playing
like we have, we'll lose.

58
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,360
What do you mean?

59
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,937
Listen, just hear me out.

60
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:48,437
We're losing because
Pegasus can read our mind.

61
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,873
Because we're working so close together.

62
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,050
That's wrong.

63
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:56,137
I mean, it's the wrong strategy for us
to be using in this particular game.

64
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:58,617
If we keep dueling with
our spirits merged,

65
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,937
Pegasus' mind-reading powers will beat us.

66
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:02,900
And if we lose, everyone loses.

67
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,120
But I have another idea.

68
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,760
Well, it had better be a good one.

69
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,800
Many lives depend on us. I know.

70
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:12,531
But I think it will work.

71
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:16,257
I think it will allow us to stop
Pegasus from reading our thoughts.

72
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,634
Tell me quickly, then.

73
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,014
I can feel Pegasus pushing at our mind.

74
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,946
Trying to probe our thoughts.

75
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,020
Okay, this is it.

76
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:27,140
Each time we play a card,
Pegasus reads our mind.

77
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:32,026
But what if we keep our minds separate
and then switch our minds back and forth?

78
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,920
Ah, switch minds.

79
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:37,697
So you're saying we won't merge
our spirits as we usually do.

80
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:42,360
Instead, we keep our thoughts
separate, secret, even from each other.

81
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,260
A dangerous move, but it
just might work. All right.

82
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,180
Let's do this!

83
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,100
Toon Summon Skull.

84
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:57,226
Emerge from the safety of Toon World and
attack the magical hat on the far left.

85
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:11,520
The Dark Magician has
performed his last trick.

86
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,280
Maybe, Pegasus.

87
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:15,640
Or maybe you're losing your touch.

88
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:17,900
Hm? What?

89
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,735
Yugi Boy's life points are unaffected?

90
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:24,402
And the Dark Magician card
is still on the field.

91
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,790
Impossible.

92
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,520
I just read his mind.

93
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:30,500
His magician had to be
hidden under that hat.

94
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:35,460
I felt him resisting my probe, but
there's no way he could have deceived me.

95
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,032
Maybe you probed the wrong mind, Pegasus.

96
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,957
One that doesn't know where
the Dark Magician hides.

97
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:41,870
Huh?

98
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:46,197
Or maybe your mind-probing powers
aren't as all-seeing as you think.

99
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,660
You dare mock the awesome
powers of my Millennium Eye?

100
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:51,900
You go too far, Yugi boy.

101
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:55,117
Hey, Taya, do you have
any idea what's going on?

102
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,906
I think it has to do
with Yugi's other spirit.

103
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,737
Yugi's somehow using the
spirit from his Millennium

104
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:04,257
Puzzle to confuse Pegasus and
block him from reading minds.

105
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:06,987
You gained nothing from
your attack, Pegasus.

106
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,817
Even with your magic,
you won't be able to win.

107
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:12,457
Because you're not the only
duelist with a Millennium Item.

108
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:17,246
Now, let's see how well your Millennium
Eye measures up to my Millennium Puzzle.

109
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:19,980
Whoa, Yugi.

110
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,317
I sure hope he knows what he's doing.

111
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:26,217
I mean, how much do any of us really
know about his Millennium Puzzle?

112
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,317
Millennium Puzzle, Millennium Schmuzzle.

113
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,197
I just wish I could help him somehow.

114
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,577
But no, all I can do is
cheer from the sidelines,

115
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:36,131
while my best buddy duels his
toughest duel all by himself.

116
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:41,700
I lay this card face down on
the field and end my turn.

117
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:47,117
Pegasus, do you know what the card is
that I just pulled and laid on the field?

118
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,847
Just use your Millennium
Eye to read my mind.

119
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,805
That is, if you think you can.

120
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,000
No problem.

121
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:57,820
You can hide nothing from me.

122
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,080
We'll see about that.

123
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:10,590
What? What?

124
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:14,351
I can't tell what that hidden
card is that you just played.

125
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:19,320
Sorry, Pegasus, but I don't know
what this face-down card is either.

126
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:22,602
Reading my mind will tell
you absolutely nothing.

127
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,800
How is he doing this?

128
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:30,020
You see, Pegasus, I don't know what that
card is because I am no longer Yugi Moto,

129
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,140
but someone else altogether.

130
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:37,095
Through the magic of the Millennium
Puzzle, two minds inhabit this body.

131
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:41,820
Now each time you try to read one of
our minds, we'll use the Mind Shuffle.

132
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:42,960
Mind Shuffle?

133
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:47,460
Told ya, Yugi's battling Pegasus
with not one, but two minds.

134
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,520
Oh, I get it.

135
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:50,797
So when Pegasus tries to
read one of his minds,

136
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,537
Yugi can switch back to the other one.

137
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,679
I guess it's true.

138
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:56,060
Two minds are better than one.

139
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,440
It's all over.

140
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:02,157
Give us back our prisoner now and we
might still let you leave in one piece.

141
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,557
Face it, you've got nowhere else to run.

142
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:05,800
Bakura, he's right.

143
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,080
So, punk, what's it gonna be?

144
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,080
You ignorant mortals.

145
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,780
It's far from all over.

146
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,717
We have barely even begun to play.

147
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,397
And I'll show you the
cards fate has dealt you.

148
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,774
Stop talking nonsense.

149
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,039
Give up right now.

150
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,979
What's with Bakura all of a sudden?

151
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,310
Wait a minute.

152
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:28,357
I think I remember him
acting like this once before.

153
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,437
It was when the evil spirit from Bakura's

154
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,857
Millennium Ring dragged us
all to the Shadow Realm.

155
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:37,397
I thought that was just a bad dream,
but it looks like it really did happen.

156
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:40,362
And it looks like that
evil Bakura is back again.

157
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:44,933
Now I'll teach you the true meaning
of fear as I summon the man-eater bug.

158
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:49,040
With the power of my Millennium Ring.

159
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,440
What's going on?

160
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,270
Oh, no!

161
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:02,237
He's brought the monster
on the car to life!

162
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:04,202
and he's going to sick it on us.

163
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:13,680
Now, you mortal fools,
prepare to meet your doom.

164
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:17,080
Here it comes!

165
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:19,750
Run!

166
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,174
Let's get out of here!

167
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:28,457
Present-day humans are so fun
to terrorize, don't you think?

168
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:29,640
No, I don't.

169
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:32,220
But then again, I am a present-day human.

170
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,614
What the heck are you?

171
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:38,640
Me, someone with great
power, soon to be greater.

172
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,977
But I can't spend the day having fun.

173
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:42,320
I have things to do.

174
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,957
So I'll summon the
morphing jar to this plane

175
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:48,520
and put an end to their pathetic whining.

176
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,040
What is that?

177
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:59,460
The jar's magic will send these
ridiculous thugs to the graveyard.

178
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,150
Whoa!

179
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,800
Where the heck are we?

180
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:14,402
And what the heck is that thing?

181
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:21,080
So, still trying to read my mind, Pegasus?

182
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:22,300
Go right ahead.

183
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,280
No thanks, Yugi boy.

184
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:27,717
My mind-scanning abilities
are only one of many

185
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:31,037
skills that I possess and
that you need to worry about.

186
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:33,767
Or have you forgotten
who invented this game?

187
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,552
Besides, I can sense that
you're prepared to switch minds.

188
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:41,837
Yes, you're ready to switch again the
moment I begin to probe your mind.

189
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:45,460
So rather than waste both our
time, let's move on, shall we?

190
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:48,597
You've still no defense
against my toon monsters,

191
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:53,268
and it's only a matter of time till I
find which hat hides your dark magician.

192
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,397
Then pick a hat,

193
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:59,737
and we'll see just how impressive your
mastery of duel monsters really is.

194
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:03,637
but i suspect that you've relied on
the magic of your millennium eye for

195
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:08,857
so long your dueling skills have
diminished even if your little theory

196
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:15,377
was true i'm still far and away a
superior duelist to you we shall see

197
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:21,580
pegasus make your next move toon
summon skull attack the middle hand

198
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:32,760
Did I get him?

199
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,040
I think I got him.

200
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,860
I must have gotten him.

201
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:38,830
No!

202
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,239
I've missed again.

203
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,160
What a shame, Pegasus.

204
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:44,620
Another turn wasted.

205
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:48,380
And for my next turn, a
quick change is in order.

206
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,760
So you've switched again.

207
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,680
That's right, Pegasus.

208
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:58,020
And our mind shuffle strategy
is working perfectly.

209
00:11:58,580 --> 00:11:59,410
Great!

210
00:11:59,493 --> 00:12:02,197
The Living Arrow card could
really turn this match around.

211
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:06,940
So, I'll just play this card face
down and I'll see you later, Pegasus.

212
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:12,309
You're looking frustrated.

213
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,697
He's played another card face down.

214
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:17,377
And there's no point in
trying to read this Yugi's

215
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:20,460
mind because he has no idea
what card it is either.

216
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,380
So, Yugi's played another card face down.

217
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:29,440
And even though I don't know what
that card is, I have faith in Yugi.

218
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:32,420
And faith in the heart of the cards.

219
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,180
I'm becoming annoyed.

220
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,240
Eureka!

221
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,960
The card that will devastate
your dark magician!

222
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:46,320
Magical Neutralizing Force, activate!

223
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:55,637
This special card acts to
eliminate any and all magic effects

224
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,037
currently active on the
opponent's field which means the

225
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,197
concealing effect of your

226
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:06,337
magical hats now disappears oh no

227
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:10,460
the magic hats are evaporating
the dark magician is revealed

228
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:15,557
it's all over for him and your life points

229
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:18,760
you can only watch as i
savor my final victory

230
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:23,980
does your heart grow cold knowing
that your demise is only moments away

231
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:28,800
Come on out, Toon Summon Skull!

232
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:30,745
Show them the face of victory!

233
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:32,790
No!

234
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:35,708
His Toon monsters are
virtually unstoppable,

235
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:38,457
and my Dark Magician
is totally unprotected!

236
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:41,297
There's nothing I can do, unless...

237
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:42,880
Toon Summon Skull!

238
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,760
Attack the Dark Magician!

239
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,400
Lightning Strike Attack!

240
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,920
Devastate his dark magician

241
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:06,860
I don't have a move, but Yugi might

242
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:12,440
Pegasus No, they've switched
again I defend my magician

243
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:18,740
With the card I played face down
The magic card, living arrow

244
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:20,950
What?

245
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,097
Your hidden card is the living arrow?

246
00:14:23,180 --> 00:14:24,160
That's right.

247
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,140
That is my secret card.

248
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:28,957
And since you're the
creator of Duel Monsters,

249
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:31,746
you must know all about
the Living Arrow card.

250
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:36,482
And how it can fuse with any card
an opponent might put into play.

251
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:41,073
And it doesn't matter whether that
card is a monster card or a magic card.

252
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,854
We've thwarted your mind-reading magic,

253
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:49,100
and now we're going to use your
very own magic card against you.

254
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:51,410
Pegasus,

255
00:14:51,493 --> 00:14:54,477
I used the Living Arrow card
to fuse with your Magical

256
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:58,340
Neutralizing card and fire
it right back at Toon World!

257
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:01,930
Hmm,

258
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:03,239
it doesn't matter,

259
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:07,321
cause it's already too late for
you to stop my Summon Skull Attack!

260
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:12,040
Your Dark Magician is vanquished!

261
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:14,760
Sorry, Pegasus!

262
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:17,120
You've forgotten my other down card!

263
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,100
It's a trap card.

264
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:23,500
And it's one of my favorites,
Mirror Force. A trap?

265
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:29,957
It deflects back, summons Skull's attack,

266
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:33,917
and since the other card neutralized the
magic that made your toons untouchable,

267
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,877
your toon monsters return to their
original form and appear on the field,

268
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,280
just in time to catch the blast.

269
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:44,840
It's impossible.

270
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:48,217
I can't believe you've
destroyed all my beloved toons.

271
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,701
This is a nightmare, a bad dream.

272
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,537
This can't truly be happening.

273
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,450
No!

274
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:58,860
We did it.

275
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,727
All the toons are destroyed.

276
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:02,920
Yes, and it was your plan, Yugi.

277
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:04,540
I'm very proud of you.

278
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:08,140
Score stands at Yugi 900, Pegasus 600.

279
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,480
Sorry, sir.

280
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,657
Yugi has proven formidable indeed,

281
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:15,505
and his Millennium item is even
more intriguing than I imagined.

282
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:16,690
All right.

283
00:16:16,773 --> 00:16:18,325
Hey, you're in the lead, Yugg.

284
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:19,500
At last!

285
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:22,637
Those creepy toon monsters
seemed almost unbeatable.

286
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,597
But I knew Yuggie'd figure
out a way to defeat them.

287
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,980
I just knew it!

288
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,400
As you can see,

289
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:34,377
there's not a single particle of those
pathetic fools left in this dimension.

290
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:37,197
I've no patience for
obstacles that get in my way.

291
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,520
Remember that. Huh?

292
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:41,617
I don't know how you did that,
and I probably don't want to know.

293
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:43,977
Just tell me who you are, what you want.

294
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:46,589
I know you're not really
our friend Bakura.

295
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,097
You're the one Yugi beat.

296
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,117
He banished you to the graveyard,

297
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:53,612
and in the process he freed
Bakura from your mind control.

298
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:57,822
Yes, but that wouldn't have happened
if Bakura hadn't betrayed me.

299
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,040
I've decided I need a new host.

300
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,857
You won't take me without
a fight. Not yours.

301
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:05,881
I want a vessel without a
mind or soul of its own.

302
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,097
You want Mokuba.

303
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,660
Now turn him over or face
the same fate as those gods.

304
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:20,060
Yugi, I'm impressed.

305
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,660
When I first met you,

306
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:25,597
you were just another boy who
showed some faint dueling promise,

307
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,640
but with my gentle guidance.

308
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,508
Well, just look at you now.

309
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:33,237
You're one step away from
becoming world champion.

310
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:37,220
You've been to the Shadow Realm
and back, and most importantly,

311
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:41,017
you've finally begun to master the
power of your Millennium Puzzle.

312
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:45,865
And you see, Yu-Gi-Boy, for me, that's
what this whole tournament has been about.

313
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,840
For I plan to take
possession of your puzzle.

314
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,440
My puzzle? No!

315
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:57,360
Yes, you and I will finish this
contest in the Shadow Realm, Yu-Gi.

316
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:00,740
And this time, it's winner take all.
